[
  {
    "id": "sitl27-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 35 Lucy in the Sky",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Lucy in the Sky: five ArduPilot copters take off, spread on a line, form a sphere, tumble the sphere around body +Y (pitch 0\u219245\u219290\u2192135\u2192180), then peel off one-by-one and land.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl27-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl27-tab",
    "name": "Lucy in the Sky \u2014 sphere tumble then peel",
    "info": "Choreography on AP sysids 1\u20135:\n1. GUIDED \u2192 arm \u2192 takeoff 40 m\n2. Spread: line spacing 18 m (fixed Canberra-home anchor, alt 40)\n3. Form sphere radius 12 m\n4. Rotate as a group around Y: pitchDeg 0 \u2192 45 \u2192 90 \u2192 135 \u2192 180 (same sphere node family, pitch on each step)\n5. Peel: sequential NAV_LAND with 2 s pacing\n\nSphere is 3-D \u2014 followers sit above and below the anchor; keep the anchor high enough (40 m with radius 12 clears ~28 m AGL).\n\nHarness: ap-arm-ready-fleet. Long wait \u2014 settle delays between geometry steps.",
    "x": 360,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
